Translation patch: libsignal-protocol `Cargo.toml`

Change: adds an empty `extraction` feature.
Why: the extraction builds the crate with this feature, which switches on the `charon` tool attributes and the `cfg` gates of the other patches.
Behaviour: unchanged. The feature is off by default.

diff --git a/rust/protocol/Cargo.toml b/rust/protocol/Cargo.toml
--- a/rust/protocol/Cargo.toml
+++ b/rust/protocol/Cargo.toml
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@ uuid = { workspace = true }
 zerocopy = { workspace = true, features = ["derive"] }
 
 [features]
+extraction = []
 kyber768 = ["libcrux-ml-kem/kyber", "libcrux-ml-kem/mlkem768"]
 # ML-KEM matches the NIST standard version of Kyber. It may still change
 # incompatibly until the final version of the standard is published and
